10. Hyper-V Dynamic Memory Issue
During boot, Rocky showed messages like:
```text
hv_balloon: Balloon request will be partially fulfilled. Balloon floor reached.
```
We identified this as a Hyper-V Dynamic Memory / balloon driver message.
Meaning:
```text
Hyper-V was trying to reclaim memory from the Rocky VM.
Rocky reached the lower memory limit it was willing to give back.
```
Decision:
```text
Disable Dynamic Memory for BAA-SML-NETH1.
Use static memory instead.
```
Final memory setting:
```text
Startup RAM: 8192 MB
Dynamic Memory: Disabled
```
Reason:
```text
NethServer will run containers and services.
Static memory is more predictable and cleaner for a server VM.
```
PowerShell verification command:
```powershell
Get-VMMemory -VMName "BAA-SML-NETH1"
```
This command shows the memory configuration for the VM.
It helps verify whether Dynamic Memory is enabled or disabled and what startup memory is assigned.
PowerShell configuration command:
```powershell
Set-VMMemory -VMName "BAA-SML-NETH1" -DynamicMemoryEnabled $false -StartupBytes 8GB
```
This command disables Dynamic Memory and sets the VM to use 8 GB of static RAM.
It removes the memory ballooning behaviour and gives Rocky/NethServer predictable memory.
