13. `nslookup` Issue
`nslookup` did not work at first.
Cause:
```text
Rocky Minimal does not always include nslookup by default.
```
Package needed:
```text
bind-utils
```
Check command:
```bash
which nslookup
```
This checks whether `nslookup` exists in the system path.
If installed, it should return something like:
```text
/usr/bin/nslookup
```
Install command:
```bash
sudo dnf install -y bind-utils
```
This installs DNS troubleshooting tools, including `nslookup`, `dig`, and `host`.
It is required for DNS testing on Rocky Minimal.
DNS test command:
```bash
nslookup google.com
```
This tests external DNS resolution.
Internal DNS test command:
```bash
nslookup baa-sml-dc1.bojieanzac.com
```
This tests AD DNS resolution for the SML domain controller.
Expected result:
```text
baa-sml-dc1.bojieanzac.com -> 172.16.50.10
```
