14. Rocky Updates and Tools
Update command:
```bash
sudo dnf update -y
```
This updates Rocky packages and security patches.
It is required before installing NethServer so the base OS is clean and current.
Reboot command:
```bash
sudo reboot
```
This restarts Rocky so updated packages, services, and any kernel updates are fully applied.
Useful tools command:
```bash
sudo dnf install -y curl wget vim bash-completion net-tools bind-utils chrony
```
This installs common admin tools.
`curl` is needed for downloading the NethServer installer. `wget` is another download tool. `vim` is a text editor. `bash-completion` improves shell usability. `net-tools` provides older network tools. `bind-utils` provides DNS tools. `chrony` provides time synchronisation.
Enable Chrony:
```bash
sudo systemctl enable --now chronyd
```
This enables and starts the Chrony time service immediately.
It is important because server logs, TLS certificates, authentication, and future AD integration all depend on correct time.
Chrony check:
```bash
chronyc tracking
```
This shows whether Chrony is tracking a time source.
It helps verify that Rocky’s time synchronisation is working.
