18. NS8 VPN CIDR Decision
We chose:
```text
10.250.0.0/24
```
Reason:
```text
It does not overlap with existing lab networks.
```
Existing networks to avoid:
```text
172.16.50.0/24    SML site
172.16.60.0/24    BIG site
172.16.70.0/24    possible EDGE site
10.8.0.0/24       OpenVPN
100.64.0.0/10     Tailscale CGNAT range
```
We clarified pfSense behaviour:
```text
For a single-node NS8 setup, pfSense usually does not need to route 10.250.0.0/24.
The server still uses 172.16.50.60 as its normal LAN address.
The 10.250.0.0/24 range is mainly for NS8 internal cluster VPN/container management.
```
If future NS8 nodes are added across sites:
```text
pfSense must allow communication between the normal LAN IPs of the nodes.
Example: 172.16.50.60 ↔ 172.16.60.x
```
